    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "ETFs and mutual funds differ primarily in how they trade and are managed. ETFs trade on stock exchanges like individual stocks, offering high intraday liquidity, whereas mutual funds are priced once daily based on the Net Asset Value (NAV). Furthermore, many ETFs are passively managed by tracking an index, while mutual funds can be actively managed by fund professionals trying to beat the market.\n\n| Feature | ETF | Mutual Fund |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Liquidity** | High (Traded all day) | Lower (Traded once daily) |\n| **Management Style**| Often Passive (Index tracking) | Can be Active or Passive |",
